        <p>ROMANCE OF A NURSE. jos) Mr. A. Mortimer Singer, a wealthy b Aniaring- alloonist and a member of the fanaous sewnove machine firm, was married on SaturdaY bride Parish Church to Miss Pillavoine• rrn Itir' was a professional nurse who attennet• ,fter Singer during his convalescence in Londone''airo le had met with an aeroplane accident, i• ll! TV in 1910, when he broke his leg in a rae",, bride and her friends lived day beL°',l wedding in Mr. Singer's yacht M°divelit-ei at Southwick, Mr. Singer staying at an ha°t Brighton. Wearing an " aeroplane." h rolve3 a grey travelling costume, the bride Ivo iiiberg' ashore for the ceremony in a dinghy hY boa of the yacht's crew. She stepPed ing stage specially built and decorated Opoicl occasion. She was given away by' Sir. na of Ferrier, the brain specialist, a great frle herself and the bridegroom.</p>
