        <p>- -- He passed his Final Law Examination tfc° months before he was 21, at the same ers' tion which our townsman, Councillor Jen' passed. Mr. Browne stayed with the old firl/1 for some seven months, and was then engagew by the late Mr. Robert Davies and Mr. Vi7i'llia° Sharp to enter their Common Law departmaelt but was subsequently very kindly released fr,fr, that engagement on the death of the late George Townend Moore (who had the princiPl Advocacy Practice in the district at that tin)..fe" and hecommenced practice in Bank-street, re' the old County Court. •. When the County Court Was closed, and 01 new one opened, he removed into his PreSefire offices in Sankey-street, now having been the over 16 years. His. principal practice has been in the lee— n se Police and County Courts, but he has bee a far North \ as the Newcastle Police Court. °rind as far South as the Lewes County court, a ,aallafrgo_re has been engaged in many noted cases. 12e3iwras. Ne.leredperbcyil Tied With Alderman Bennett fh the He civ.eetri---toe majority ley Ward, but at the d fth en o e three years desir 6 retire, owing to pressure of business. Ile Nv“ induced at the last moment to be again noinin- ated against the present Alderman Bennet!, when the election resulted in a tie, each mai' date receiving 419 votes, and at the conclusiq of the counting the late Alderman Francofln? gave his casting vote for Mr. Bennett. It 0, only fair to add that Mr. Bennett pressed fa` a new contest to be held, but Mr. Broe've declined. gr. At the time of the non-trading question, Browne was induced by the leaders of bein parties to try and wrest the, seat for the TO: Hall Ward from Councillor' Lord, but after severe contest he was defeated by 45 votes. - He is one of the senior life governors of 14 Warrington Infirmary, and is chairman a Warrington Dramatic Society, and 1100301 treasurer, and has been .connected with society for over 30 years. He is :the onlY 110 manent trustee of the "Thomas N:ernst- Charity, and during the 13 years of its e,-the ence he has conducted all the details ca,,eoa Trust without any fee or reward, and has " of the means of distributing over 1,200 pai,„l.Biog blankets and over 400 articles of warm ele"-- among the old women lof Warrington.</p>
