      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-10-25_WidnesExaminer_art0220" n="art0220">
        <head>LORD WOLM ER'S VISIT. Penketh School Sale of Work.</head>
        <p>LORD WOLM ER'S VISIT. Penketh School Sale of Work.</p>
        <p>A. two days' sale of work to pay off a debt incurred in extending the Penketh Infants' School, was held on Thursday and yesterday in the Sankey Schools..</p>
        <p>The sal:- was opened on Thursday by Lord Wolmer, M.P. The Rev. J. R. Jones presided, and there were also on the platform Mr. W. Furness, Mr. H. Fairclough, Mr. F. Dayies (secretary), Mr. F. T. Newbold and Mr. E. Rum- bill (churchwardens). Miss Tinsley was the treasurer. The stallholders were :--</p>
        <p>G.F.S. Flower and Crockery Stall.—Mesdames Dutton, Fairclough, Foster and James Wray. the Misses Jones and Gorse, assisted by the members of the branch.</p>
        <p>Teachers' Stall.—Mrs. Murray, the Misses Murray, Standish and Ansdell.</p>
        <p>Congregational Stall.—Mesdames Furness,</p>
        <p>lluxtable, Cooke, Wray, Hill, 'Toward, 11013111 and E. Dunibill. • ft, Refreshment Stall.—Mesdames Wolsteno,°4, Wilkinson, Clark, Woods; Oakley, Wrench, nett and Smith, the Misses Wolstencroft, Jojl• son and Fairclough. rt Sankey Guild Stall.—lllesdames Gorse, P. Davies and Kilshaw, Misses 1311"-1 Gilbert and Kilsliaw. The Chairman said that the school had 'Ai-to extended' 12 months ago, and the rtlGO the contractor. That sale was to clear "</p>
        <p>debt off. Lord Wolmer said they were proud 0,.A way, in which Churchpeople every year 811,7,eir every place Were continuously putting hands in their pockets to maintain the C181:44 schools. It was only by such great efforts if' that that the money could be raised, and ev!:,,,,,* one 'there was co-operating heartily to br'ff. about such a result as they saw that da)". was incumbent upon them to keep in rePair„d munificent gifts of those pious Church men women who had gone before. (Applause.). Mr. W. Furness proposed a vote of 1,1'41 Mr. 11. Fairclough secohded. Lord Woliner,4s received_ an orchid buttonhole from little -</p>
        <p>Betty Foster, suitably replied. - Yesterday's proceedings will be found 011 other page.</p>
