        <p>ing on the visitors' left resulted in Cox testing Holmes, when the latter saved smartly. The visitors continued to have the best of the game, their halfbacks giving splendid kiwi-oft to their forwards, and the home backs conceded a fruit- less corner. The home players now improved, and had a turn at the visitors' end, where faulty kicking by Holmes, the visitors' back, allowed the home forwards to become dangerous on several,occasions. Only the smartness of Rigby between the posts saved his side from down- fall. After a spell of midfield play, Pritchard opened the score. From the centre kick both teams played finely, and each end was visited in turn, but no further scoring was recordod before the interval.</p>
        <p>ter, T. Caldwell and J. W. Allen. Reserves: J. Lawless and J. Whittaker.</p>
        <p>Latchford Atheltic (selected from).—W. Crad- dick, Crozier, Evans, Brooks, Dickinson, Cains, Massey, J. Brooks, Dunbobbin, Hall, Little - wood, T. Edwards D. Morris. Padgate United play Risley A.F.C. at Risley. Padgate United team: R. Nork; J. Warburton did J. Holcroft; W. Hodgkinson, W. Spencer and R. Hankinson; James Houghton, A. Derby- shire, John Houghton, J. Rigby and S. Hard- man. -</p>
