        <p>Tenders. COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. The Sanitary Works Committee are ..pre- pared to receive TENDERS for : /V STEAM-DRIVEN PUMP, to deliver 9,000 gallons of water per hour; Also TENDERS for COVERING 4, STEAM- JACKETTED DRYERS, 6ft.. 6in. dia- meter by 13ft..long. Further information may be obtained from the undersigned. The. Contractor whose Tender is accepted will be required to observe the recognised customs and conditions as to rate of wages and working hours prevailing within the district. Tenders, securely fastened, must be addressed: "The Chairman, Sanitary Works Committee, Town Hall, Warrington, endorsed "Tender for Pump,' or " Tender for Covering," and delivered' not later than Saturday,"lst Novem- ber, 1913. The .Igwest or any Tender will not necessarily be accented. R. WILSON, Manager. Longford Depot, Warrington, 22nd October, 1913.</p>
        <p>likfßS. ELIZABETH DOI3SON, Deceased.— in. All persons having any debts, claims, or de- mands against the estate of Elizabeth Dobson. late of Black Bear House, Latchford, Warrington. widow, who died on the, 16th instant. aie requested to send particulars thereof, in writing, at. once to us. the undersigned, the solicitors to the Executors. Dated this 23rd .day- of October, 1913. ROBERT DAVIES &amp; CO., Market-place, Warrington.</p>
        <p>TO THE ELECTORS OF ST. AUSTIN'S WARD. LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,— At the request of a number of influential Ratepayers in this Ward, both Conservative and Liberal, as testified in part by my Nomination Papers, I have consented to allow myself to be nominated to stand as an absolutely Independent Candidate kir the St. Austin's Ward Election. I have been a Resident and Occupier of my Present Offices in Sankey-street, together for 26 years, and am therefore fully cognizant of all the needs of the Ward. If elected I shall net in Council and in Com- mittee Kithout regard to Polities in ahy WY What" ever, but will only act and vote for the best Inter- ests of the whole of the Ratepayers of my Native _Town. My Office is most conveniently situated in the centre of the Ward, so that at all times I can be approached by any of the Burgesses on any real grievance they may have. I am entirely in favour of all Corporetion Employees having "A Fair Day's Wage for a Fair Day's Work," and Reasonable and Proper Pay for Overtime. Yours faithfully, ARTHUR BROWNE. 67, Sankey-street, Warrington. 23rd October, 1913. T° THE ELECTORS OF WHITECROSS WARD. LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,— My term of office as one of your representa- tives on the Town Council expires in November next. It is my intention to again ask for your support in order that I may continue to serve you, I trust to your satisfaction. Since you honoured me with your support in February, 1907, I have applied myself to the work and duties connected with municipal life, and I have striven to do all in my. power for. the good</p>
